{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/522224-what-do-vampires-want","id":522224,"title":"What do Vampires want?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-20T12:26:38-07:00","id":522224,"title":"What do Vampires want?","content":"This seems to come up a lot in Vampire games... PCs come to some authority figure (or even just an ally), and say they want help with something. Their potential ally says &quot;Ahh, but in exchange for what?&quot; And the player characters say &quot;What do you want?&quot;<br /> <br /> (Okay, often I'll turn that question around and say &quot;What do you have to offer?&quot;, but the essence remains the same)<br /> <br /> So I figured I'd start brainstorming some things Vampires might want in return for a favour, from the big to the small. Or, to flip it around, what useful things can your vampire offer as payment to another?<br /> <br /> - A future favour (okay, this is kind of a cop-out, but probably a pretty frequent thing)<br /> - Inside information about someone they're close to<br /> - A person - whether a favored vessel or a ghoul retainer<br /> - Concession of territory/feeding grounds<br /> - Some hard to obtain physical object<br /> - Tutoring in a Clan-specific Discipline<br /> - &quot;Drink my blood...just once...for now&quot;<br /> - Taking action against another Vampire (&quot;I need you to send Vinnie a message...&quot;)<br /> - Using your Disciplines on their behalf (&quot;I've got this inconvenient mortal acquaintance...I hear you can erase memories?&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T12:49:15-07:00","id":522332,"title":"","content":"The left finger of a black haired woman born on the 7th of May, because it's precisely what I need for a powerful Theban Sorcery working. <br /> <br /> Meth. As much as you can get me. Right now. <br /> <br /> Your assistance in a con. I need someone to distract some guy while I sneak in and ghoul his kid. <br /> <br /> Kill person x. Sooner is better. Make sure she *stays* dead. Don't ask - I thought I killed her four times; I saw her walking only days after every time. She's not one of us, but she might well have other .. abilities .. most people don't have. <br /> <br /> Keep this amulet safe for the next two weeks. Don't ever touch it with your bare skin - I don't expect the last vampire who did to arise from torpor anytime soon. <br /> <br /> Here, get rid of this. Yes, of course it's a body. You don't need to know the specifics. <br /> <br /> Vote for me in the next Carthian elections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T13:31:08-07:00","id":522380,"title":"","content":"Say nice things about me in Elysium around specific visitors.<br /> Say nasty things about me in Elysium around specific visitors.<br /> Pay off this beat cop. Careful he doesn't get suspicious and shoot you.<br /> Tag this building with this mark. Destroy the post-it note when you're done.<br /> <br /> How difficult (or dangerous, or puzzling) the task is should depend on what the debt-holding vampire needs at present and thinks they might need in future. An easy repayment is good if they want the PC to come back for another favour sometime soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T13:33:35-07:00","id":522385,"title":"","content":"I need some of your blood man, not all, just a pint or two. Don't mind why, you owe me it.<br /> <br /> You see we can't coexist so it needs to be gone. Silver is a fine metal, at least according to legend. Yes of course it's a werewolf!<br /> <br /> You see I care for her, she just needs somewhere to sleep for a few nights. And damn don't drink from her or something stupid, she knows nothing of us.<br /> <br /> You know the Harpy right? Please it would be nice if you introduce me to her.<br /> <br /> You know the thing you did with Mont\u00e9 ? Yeah, it was a bit hard on my business and i need a formal apology.<br /> <br /> What do you know about Lloyd? Tell me.<br /> <br /> You know the Dragons been up to some shit-weird experiments on some magical nexus in this city. Well the dead won't stay dead on Enfield Cemetery and i want you to keep the masquerade around the graveyard for a month and a day.<br /> <br /> I really don't know why i did that, but you owe me so you clean it up.<br /> <br /> I need to know where the haven yo your sire is and i need you to shut your month about this little talk.<br /> <br /> I need you to find a mortal. Preferably a blond accountant in his early thirties with a martial interest. If i'm going to ghoul him or not is not of your business.<br /> <br /> You have some contacts in the field of &lt;inssert field&gt; that usually help you out right? I need you to introduce me to them and ask them to do me a favor on your behalf.<br /> <br /> You have a car right? That's really very nice, may I have the keys to it?<br /> <br /> You see a favored ally of mine has fallen to the eternal sleep of ages and left a newly embraced childe that i vowed to my patronage and responsibility to her, but the Prince has granted me a great boon of embracing a childe of my own, therefor I need you to take full responisbility for her until she's released. I figured you're a good choice, after all you're of the same clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T22:27:46-07:00","id":522936,"title":"","content":"I'd also say that, at least during the initial stages of interaction, a lot of vampires probably give the person they're dealing with some make work. Just to see if they follow their orders, how well they follow them and the like. So it could be some minor things like,<br /> <br /> Without looking inside this briefcase, deliver it to this address tomorrow at exactly midnight.<br /> Drive me from here to here, take the quickest route.<br /> I need you to look after this person for a week, talk to them, but never mention me.<br /> <br /> However, all of these are just tests. The briefcase has nothing important inside, there is no urgency to the drive and the person is the other vampires Ghoul or retainer. The one giving the favour just wants to see how loyal and, or, intelligent the person asking for a favour is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T05:34:13-07:00","id":524290,"title":"","content":"I need you to break into the museum of natural history and steal an item of occult power.<br /> <br /> Get the baron to call off her feud with me.<br /> <br /> Someone has been writing a screenplay that hits a little too close to the truth. The Invictus want the script destroyed and the source silenced. Do this service and you will be granted a title and domain.<br /> <br /> That warehouse down by the docks? Yeah, burn it down along with anyone in it.<br /> <br /> A fellow clan member has gone missing. Find him and I'll owe you a boon.<br /> <br /> Do you believe in ghosts? A recent acquisition of mine needs exorcising, and I don't mean the kind you get from DVDs.<br /> <br /> A member of the Ordo has made a mistake. Unfortunately, that mistake is loose in the city. Clean it up and you'll have the gifts of the covenant on your side.<br /> <br /> Find my errant childe and bring him home. He's one breach of the Masquerade away from getting both of us staked by the prince.<br /> <br /> (Bonus points if you get the references <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1257,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","user":"Kerensky","date":". 05-22-2015, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T05:45:10-07:00","id":524294,"title":"","content":"It's exorcise, by the way. With an O.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T05:56:09-07:00","id":524301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/522224-what-do-vampires-want?p=524294#post524294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's exorcise, by the way. With an O.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fixed. Damn computer, thinking that it's smarter than I am.\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T06:31:54-07:00","id":524337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/522224-what-do-vampires-want?p=524290#post524290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need you to break into the museum of natural history and steal an item of occult power.<br /> <br /> Get the baron to call off her feud with me.<br /> <br /> Someone has been writing a screenplay that hits a little too close to the truth. The Invictus want the script destroyed and the source silenced. Do this service and you will be granted a title and domain.<br /> <br /> That warehouse down by the docks? Yeah, burn it down along with anyone in it.<br /> <br /> A fellow clan member has gone missing. Find him and I'll owe you a boon.<br /> <br /> Do you believe in ghosts? A recent acquisition of mine needs exorcising, and I don't mean the kind you get from DVDs.<br /> <br /> A member of the Ordo has made a mistake. Unfortunately, that mistake is loose in the city. Clean it up and you'll have the gifts of the covenant on your side.<br /> <br /> Find my errant childe and bring him home. He's one breach of the Masquerade away from getting both of us staked by the prince.<br /> <br /> (Bonus points if you get the references <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most of them are VtM:B. But the last ones.. hm..?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T07:13:06-07:00","id":524403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/522224-what-do-vampires-want?p=524337#post524337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Most of them are VtM:B. But the last ones.. hm..?</div> </div> </div> </div> The last two are from VtM:B as well, just slightly modified to fit Requiem. The Ordo one is the quest from Strauss to kill the gargoyle. Sub in the Ordo for the Tremere (both creepy cults).<br /> <br /> The other is the quest from Isaac to go talk to Ash and get him to go back to him. In the news reports, there's the story where Ash survived yet another horrible car accident.\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T08:39:27-07:00","id":524500,"title":"","content":"I think the Circle of the Crone are closer to requiem Tremere. <br /> <br /> If it was the Ordo they would probably <i>be</i> the mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T09:38:51-07:00","id":524536,"title":"","content":"See, I always saw the Ordo Dracul as <i><b>More Tremere </b></i>than the Crone in style and flavor. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T02:37:40-07:00","id":525307,"title":"","content":"I'm on board of the boat which says Ordo is the new Tremere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T06:48:00-07:00","id":525433,"title":"","content":"When I first read the Ordo, my first thought was &quot;the bastard love child of the Tremere and Tziminscee without broken mechanics.&quot; So, +1 thoughts for the above from me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}